\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Eligibility, original selection, and whole-view support are separate decisions. (a) A complete child call runs on frozen $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle P$}\mathaccent "0362{P}_2$; its own prediction $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle P$}\mathaccent "0362{P}_3$ may differ from original C/U output $P_3$. An accepted buffer keeps its original identity across producer exit and fencing. Matching selected $P_2$ confirms the input; durable sync precedes installation and use. (b) Losing view support does not refute an unknown future input or authorize its commit. This is a causal native schematic, with complete-state and execution assumptions from Section~\ref {sec:contract}, not a measured timeline.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:protocol}{{2}{5}{Eligibility, original selection, and whole-view support are separate decisions. (a) A complete child call runs on frozen $\widehat P_2$; its own prediction $\widehat P_3$ may differ from original C/U output $P_3$. An accepted buffer keeps its original identity across producer exit and fencing. Matching selected $P_2$ confirms the input; durable sync precedes installation and use. (b) Losing view support does not refute an unknown future input or authorize its commit. This is a causal native schematic, with complete-state and execution assumptions from Section~\ref {sec:contract}, not a measured timeline}{figure.2}{}}
